-- title:
--   Eigencharacter at raised level Nq' of a normalised eigenform
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ and $q'$ be natural numbers with $N \neq 0$ and $Nq' \neq 0$, let $q'$ be prime with $q' \nmid N$, and let $f$ be a weight-$2$ cusp form for $\Gamma_0(N)$ which is a normalised eigenform in the sense of the structure `IsNormalizedEigenform`: its $q$-expansion coefficients $a_n =$ `qCoeff f n` satisfy $a_1 = 1$, $a_{mn} = a_m a_n$ whenever $m$ and $n$ are coprime, $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}} - p\,a_{p^r}$ for primes $p \nmid N$, and $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}}$ for primes $p \mid N$. Then there exists a ring homomorphism $\chi_1$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra (N * q') 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ N * q'}`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(Nq'))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin 2` attached to primes $\ell \nmid Nq'$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to primes $q \mid Nq'$ outside the excluded set — the excluded set being all divisors of $Nq'$, so that only the $T_\ell$ with $\ell \nmid Nq'$ occur — to the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$, such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid Nq'$ the image $\chi_1(T_\ell)$, viewed in $\mathbb{C}$, equals `qCoeff f ℓ`.
--
--   This provides the eigencharacter of the $q'$-old copy of $f$ at level $Nq'$: the degeneracy inclusion $S_2(\Gamma_0(N)) \hookrightarrow S_2(\Gamma_0(Nq'))$ carries a normalised eigenform to a simultaneous eigenvector of all $T_\ell$ with $\ell \nmid Nq'$, with the same eigenvalues $a_\ell(f)$, which are algebraic integers. It feeds the level-raising step [`CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform.exists_isNewAt_congr_of_levelRaisingCongruence`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform.exists_isNewAt_congr_of_levelRaisingCongruence).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_IsNormalizedEigenform_exists_heckeAlgebraChar_raisedLevel.lean

import Definitions.Def_FLTPrelim_Modularity
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform.exists_heckeAlgebraChar_raisedLevel
    {N q' : ℕ} [NeZero N] (hq' : q'.Prime) (hq'N : ¬ q' ∣ N) [NeZero (N * q')]
    {f : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2} (hf : CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform f) :
    ∃ χ₁ : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra (N * q') 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ N * q'} →+* integralClosure ℤ ℂ,
      ∀ (ℓ : ℕ) (hℓ : ℓ.Prime) (hℓM : ¬ ℓ ∣ N * q'),
        ((χ₁ (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T hℓ hℓM hℓM) : integralClosure ℤ ℂ) : ℂ)
          = ModularFormClass.qCoeff f ℓ := by sorry
